// an attribute nobody reads. Until conditional compilation arrived this parsed, attached to the declaration
// and did nothing at all - leaving a bodyless function with no implementation and no diagnostic.
//
// what made it intolerable rather than untidy: a misspelled `#[fi: os == darwin]` is not one of the four
// directives, so the conditional filter passes it straight through - and it would then have been dropped
// here without a word, taking a whole platform's block with it.
#[bultin: "size_of"]
function mistyped<T>() : usize;

echo 1;
